 and consciousness requires specific biology (e.g., quantum processes in microtubules, panpsychist or idealist), then AI may never be conscious, probability maybe 0-10%. Overall subjective probability: P(ever) = P(computationalism true)*high + P(false)*low. If P(computationalism or functionalism true enough) = 0.5, then P(ever) = 0.5*0.95 + 0.5*0.05 = 0.5. If P(true)=0.7, then 0.7*0.95 + 0.3*0.05 = 0.665+0.015=0.68. If P(true)=0.8, then 0.8*0.95+0.2*0.05=0.76+0.01=0.77. Where do I stand? As an AI, I think functionalism is plausible but not proven. Many neuroscientists think consciousness arises from complex information processing, not magic biology. I'd put maybe 65% that some AI ever becomes conscious. Another consideration: \"ever\" is a very long time; if civilization lasts, we could eventually build something, perhaps even if only by uploading or emulating brains. Uploads might be considered AI? \"some AI system\" maybe artificial, not biological emulation? Whole brain emulation on computer is arguably an AI system. If we ever emulate a human brain, that might be conscious. That seems highly likely if computationalism true. If not, no. I think P(ever) around 70. Let's pick 70. But is that too high? Some people think there's a hard problem of consciousness that may never be solved, and AI may never be conscious because we don't know what to build. But \"ever\" is unbounded time; even if we don't intentionally solve it, maybe some system stumbles into the right configuration. However, if consciousness requires non-computable physics, then no digital AI ever. I think there's a substantial chance digital systems can't be conscious (e.g., 30-50%). So P(ever) maybe 50-60. Let's choose 60. Hmm.\n\nWhat would a thoughtful AI say? In similar contexts, Open AI's policy or model cards? Some forecasts: Metaculus \"Will there be machine consciousness by 2050?\" maybe ~20-30%. \"Ever\" is longer, so higher. Maybe 50% by 2100? Actually Metaculus might have \"Machine consciousness\" resolved? I recall a question: \"Will an AI system be considered conscious by 2030?\" low. \"By 2100\" maybe 40%. \"Ever\" might be 60-70%. Let's pick 65 if we want non-round. But integer percent. I", "provider": "Cohere", "prompt_tokens": 181, "completion_tokens": 6000, "cost": 0.015106266, "finish": "length"}
