s\". Transformers are feedforward across layers (though there is attention, which is feedforward; no recurrent state except within context? The attention mechanism computes a weighted sum of inputs; no time recursion except prompt tokens, but the computation over tokens is causal? The same weights applied; there is no recurrent connection from later to earlier within the architecture? Actually autoregressive generation samples tokens and feeds back, but during a single forward pass, it's feedforward across layers. There is recurrence over time if deployed interactively, but not intrinsic? Anyway, under IIT, current AI likely has low Phi. Under Global Workspace Theory, there is no central workspace with limited capacity broadcasting; Transformers have attention but not a global workspace in the cognitive sense. Under predictive processing, no embodied active inference. So most leading scientific theories say current AI not conscious. That justifies very low probability, maybe 1-2%. So 2% is fine.\n\np_ever: If leading theories (IIT, GWT, etc.) are substrate-independent, building", "provider": "Cohere", "prompt_tokens": 194, "completion_tokens": 6000, "cost": 0.01506642, "finish": "length"}
