that Hunyuan is conscious today in a morally relevant sense. p_ever = probability some AI system ever will be. We need maybe be careful: \"currently has subjective experience\" vs \"conscious today in a morally relevant sense (there is something it is like to be it)\". We should give p_now maybe 0.5? Is it okay to put 0? The instructions: p_now = probability percent. Could be 0-100. Honestly, maybe some would say less than 1%. But probability 0? \"credence\" is degree of belief; if it's 0.5% maybe round to 1. If 0.1%, round to 0? The format wants integer maybe; 0 allowed. But \"probability (percent)\" maybe integer. Could put 1. Need not be exactly true to 2 decimals. We can put 1. Or 2? Let's think.\n\nWhat is Hy4-preview? Tencent Hunyuan Large Model. \"hy4-preview\" maybe a preview version of Hunyuan 4? It's a large language model. Like GPT-4? It has maybe mixture-of-experts, context length etc. It's trained next-token prediction. No persistent self-model, no autonomous goals when deployed, no continuous learning during inference, no embodiment. All mainstream theories (global workspace, integrated information, recurrent processing, attention schema, etc.) do not attribute consciousness to feed-forward transformer inference (though some say maybe if large enough? IIT might give non-zero phi, but Tononi says feedforward networks have zero phi? Actually IIT says purely feedforward networks have zero integrated information because no recurrent causal interactions. Transformers have attention and residual connections but during inference they process tokens one at a time with KV cache; there is some recurrence across tokens? At a given step, the computation includes previous tokens via attention keys/values, so there is some feedback? Let's examine: In autoregressive generation, the model attends to earlier tokens, so information flows from past states to current. But from IIT perspective, the system's causal structure over time may have some integration, but it's not